msgstr "Format of the new subtitles: "

#: gui/gui.py:301
msgid ""
"The format of your new subtitles. SRT is the most common format and is "
"supported by most video players."
msgstr ""
"The format of your new subtitles. SRT is the most common format and is "
"supported by most video players."

#: gui/gui.py:302
msgid "Edit subtitles before muxing: "
msgstr "Edit subtitles before muxing: "

#: gui/gui.py:302
msgid ""
"Before exchanging the subtitles with the new ones, the program will pause"
" so that you can edit them. The program continues after pressing <Enter> "
"in the console."
msgstr ""
"Before exchanging the subtitles with the new ones, the program will pause"
" so that you can edit them. The program continues after pressing <Enter> "
"in the console."

#: gui/gui.py:303
msgid "Save images of PGS subtitles: "
msgstr "Save images of PGS subtitles: "

#: gui/gui.py:303
msgid ""
"You can save the images that make up the old subtitles. This can be "
"useful if you want to compare the old and new subtitles. They are stored "
"in a directory where this program is installed."
msgstr ""
"You can save the images that make up the old subtitles. This can be "
"useful if you want to compare the old and new subtitles. They are stored "
"in a directory where this program is installed."

#: gui/gui.py:304
msgid "Keep original MKV files: "
msgstr "Keep original MKV files: "

#: gui/gui.py:304
msgid ""
"You can keep the original video files. This way you can test different "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"You can keep the original video files. This way you can test different "
"settings."

#: gui/gui.py:305
msgid "Keep a copy of the old subtitle files: "
msgstr "Keep a copy of the old subtitle files: "

#: gui/gui.py:305
msgid ""
"You can save the original subtitle files. This way the program does not "
"need to extract them again if you run the program again."
msgstr ""
"You can save the original subtitle files. This way the program does not "
"need to extract them again if you run the program again."

#: gui/gui.py:306
msgid "Keep a copy of the new subtitle files: "
msgstr "Keep a copy of the new subtitle files: "

#: gui/gui.py:306
msgid ""
"You can save the new subtitle files. This way you can easily edit them "
"later."
msgstr ""
"You can save the new subtitle files. This way you can easily edit them "
"later."

#: gui/gui.py:307
msgid "Use different languages for some subtitles: "
msgstr "Use different languages for some subtitles: "

#: gui/gui.py:308
msgid "help.language"
msgstr ""
"Here you can tell the program to use a different language for some "
"languages. This can be useful if the English subtitles contain letters "
"like ä, ö or ü. Then you could use the German language because it "
"contains all letters of the English language + these special letters. "
"Changes are seperated by a new line and follow this format: \"old "
"language\" -> \"new language\" (e.g. eng -> ger)."

#: gui/gui.py:309
msgid "Allowed text color brightness deviation: "
msgstr "Allowed text color brightness deviation: "

#: gui/gui.py:310
msgid "help.brightness"
msgstr ""
"You can change the maximum allowed difference in brightness in the text "
"color. This can be useful because some subtitle images are more noisy "
"than others. The value should be as low as possible but the text in the "
"images should not be too thin."

